  "decision_logic": [
    "GUARD (BLOCK): if the frozen panel or the committed Phase 16-A resolved sector map is missing/empty, OR the resolved grouping covers < 95% of the current champion universe, OR the recompute cannot reproduce the frozen composite_sn with the ORIGINAL sectors (max_abs_err > 1e-04 OR reproduction Spearman < 0.9999) -> BLOCKED_DATA_MISSING. The repaired comparison cannot be trusted.",
    "FAIL (RESEARCH_REVALIDATION_FAILED) if the repaired-sector candidate is not a valid standalone alpha under proper sectors - ANY of: candidate IC t-stat < 2.0 (statistically weak); OR candidate IC t-stat sign flips vs the champion; OR candidate net-25bps spread <= 0.0000; OR candidate net-50bps spread <= 0.0000 (not cost-robust); OR a subperiod (pre-2020 / 2020+) IC or spread sign reversal that held under the champion. The champion is HELD (not replaced); deeper research is required.",
    "KEEP (KEEP_CURRENT_PAPER_CHAMPION) if the repaired candidate is valid BUT essentially indistinguishable from the champion (full-panel Spearman >= 0.98 AND Top25 overlap >= 0.90 AND Top50 overlap >= 0.90): repaired sectors do not materially change the book, so no separate challenger is warranted - keep running the single champion.",
    "ELIGIBLE (PAPER_CHALLENGER_ELIGIBLE) otherwise: the repaired candidate is statistically strong (IC t >= 2.0, same sign), cost-robust (net-25bps > 0 and net-50bps > 0), regime-stable (no subperiod sign reversal), and MATERIALLY DIFFERENT from the champion (Spearman < 0.98 or overlap < 0.90). It becomes eligible to run as a PARALLEL PAPER CHALLENGER only - the champion is NOT replaced and nothing is promoted to live."
  ],
